From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Darren Shepherd <darren@obot.ai>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 17:55:12 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(control): a ghostty pane knows the directory it started
 in (KD-22)

ControlCore pre-seeds the terminal's working directory from the profile's
startingDirectory the moment it is constructed (GH#8969, ControlCore.cpp:112),
so the pane has an answer before the shell has said anything. GhosttyControlCore
seeded the title the same way but not the directory, leaving
ICoreState::WorkingDirectory empty until an OSC arrived - and, before the
libghostty patch in this release, forever.

The consumers that fall back to the profile's own setting when the control has
nothing (TerminalPage's duplicate-tab and split paths) were unaffected either
way. The one that does not is the suggestions palette, which passes
control.WorkingDirectory() through as the context for a recall
(AppActionHandlers.cpp:1449).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/cascadia/TerminalControl/GhosttyControlCore.cpp | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/cascadia/TerminalControl/GhosttyControlCore.cpp b/src/cascadia/TerminalControl/GhosttyControlCore.cpp
index 5a723a2f0..b79502edc 100644
--- a/src/cascadia/TerminalControl/GhosttyControlCore.cpp
+++ b/src/cascadia/TerminalControl/GhosttyControlCore.cpp
@@ -42,6 +42,13 @@ namespace winrt::Microsoft::Terminal::Control::implementation
         if (_settings)
         {
             _title = _settings.StartingTitle();
+
+            // GH#8969, the same pre-seed cascadia does: until the shell reports
+            // a directory the pane's is the one it was started in. Without this
+            // a duplicated tab or split off a ghostty pane opens wherever the
+            // profile says rather than where the pane actually is, and it stays
+            // wrong for as long as the shell reports nothing.
+            _workingDirectory = _settings.StartingDirectory();
         }
 
         Connection(connection);
